>> title: Crispy Chickpeas
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: chickpeas, roast, snack, crunch, vegan
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: crispy chickpeas, crunchy chickpeas, roasted chickpeas, spiced chickpeas, chickpea crunch, garbanzo crunch
>> pairs-with: tahini-sauce, tabbouleh
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — they are glass-crisp for about an hour and chewy by the next morning; five minutes back in a hot oven half fixes it and nothing fixes it entirely
>> step.1: pat them dry until they squeak
>> step.2: roast 400°F (200°C) 35 min, plain
>> step.3: stir the spice while they roast
>> step.4: toss hot, off the sheet

Roll @cooked chickpeas{3%cups}(510 g; drained, from two 15-oz tins) between towels until the loose skins come away, then spread them out and ~dry{20%min}. They should squeak against the cloth. Every drop of water left on a chickpea is water the oven has to boil off before it can start crisping anything, and the skins that stay on go leathery instead of crackly.

Toss @&(~1)dried chickpeas{} with @olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and ~roast{35%min} at 400°F (200°C) on a bare #sheet pan{}, shaking it twice, until they rattle like gravel and one crushed against the pan shatters rather than squashing. **Nothing else goes in the oven with them.**

Stir @smoked paprika{2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @cayenne{1/4%tsp} and @kosher salt{1%tsp} together while they roast.

Toss @&(~2)roasted chickpeas{} with @&(~1)spice{} straight off the sheet, then leave them uncovered in a single layer to cool. This is the whole argument of the file: paprika and cumin are ground seed and dried fruit, and thirty-five minutes at 400°F turns them to carbon and bitterness. On the way out they hit oil that is still hot enough to bloom them and nothing more. Store them in a paper bag, never a sealed tub — trapped steam is what makes them chewy by morning.
